    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable matchups against sub-par arms. The premier play of the day is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55), who benefits from an ideal combination of a weak opposing starter (Lorenzen, 4.82 xERA) and the favorable hitter\u2019s environment. Close behind in projected impact is **Jackson Merrill** (71.50) and **Nasim Nunez** (70.92); despite **Nasim Nunez** batting eighth, his matchup against the vulnerable Lorenzen\u2014combined with the park factor\u2014makes him a high-floor play. **Heliot Ramos** (67.31) also secures a strong spot, as his leadoff role and the exploitable matchup against Avila offset the minor drag of a catcher with an elite arm.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.60) on the bench. While his pedigree is undisputed, his efficiency score was dragged down by the matchup against Rasmussen (3.34 xERA), a hurdle that our active infielders like **Curtis Mead** and **Brayan Rocchio** do not face. We are prioritizing the higher situational ceilings of **Curtis Mead** (63.58) and **Brayan Rocchio** (64.85), both of whom benefit significantly from facing starters with xERAs north of 4.80. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) remains in the lineup despite the tough matchup against Wheeler because his baseline production is too vital to bench, though he serves as a cautionary note today; his 53.52 score reflects a significant hit due to Wheeler's elite skill. Managers should note that while **Cole Carrigg** (53.99) faces an elite arm in Palmquist, his switch-hitting utility and positional versatility keep him active in a crowded outfield, even as he lingers near the bottom of our efficiency threshold.",
